{"title":"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Back in 1802, the town idiot of Boratsville, Thungar the Stenchiﬁed, bought some apples from a vendor at the market. He paid 12 cents for the apples, but when he saw how small the apples were, he demanded two extra apples for free, and the vendor agreed. Ultimately, the price Thungar paid was one penny less per dozen apples than he would have paid had he not received the extra apples. How many apples did Thungar purchase (including the two extra)?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's say he took <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> apples. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> apples for 12 cents is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b9ae99d80e0884d5f9a0089d6e8859a90002f33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{144}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" /> cents a dozen. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/faef3f20663194a7f042daba32ca9fb69cd01f1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> apples for 12 cents is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f23f2cb708e8af87a8bf221c0ed5a721ed4cead2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{144}{a+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"43\" height=\"38\" /> cents a dozen. Their difference is 1, so we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a47ecd5dee670f0c070a4d9361024d0100b8bf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{144}{a+2}+1=\\frac{144}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/685640ce914d18eaceaab60bddf54e300dbff441.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144a+a^2+2a=144a+288$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"227\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c2f9f84e0fdafb1f85ca389ccc2877e65d5c5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+2a-288=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee9154cccb7ea36fe4b025e3badc07044dd0f4e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{-2\\pm\\sqrt{4+1152}}{2}=\\frac{-2\\pm 34}{2}=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"299\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore he bought <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/707b150be2f7a929f705d880caa88481445f9a87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> apples total.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST\">2007 Alabama ARML TST</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.p